 role in tumorigenesis</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>2001</year><volume>98</volume><fpage>10983</fpage><lpage>10985</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11572954</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.211430998</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nakayama</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Ikebe</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Beppu</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Shirasuna</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>High expression levels of NF&#x003ba;B, I&#x003ba;B&#x003b1; and Akt kinase in squamous cell carcinoma of the oral cavity</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>2001</year><volume>92</volume><fpage>3037</fpage><lpage>3044</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11753981</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/1097-0142(20011215)92:12&#x0003c;3037::AID-CNCR10171&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-#</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sun</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Paciga</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Feldman</surname><given-names>RI</given-names></name><name><surname>Yuan</surname><given-names>ZQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ma</surname><given-names>XL</given-names></name><name><surname>Shelley</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Jove</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsichlis</surname><given-names>PN</given-names></name><name><surname>Nicosia</surname><given-names>SV</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>AKT1/PKB&#x003b1; kinase is frequently elevated in human cancers and its constitutive activation is required for oncogenic transformation in NIH3T3 cells</article-title><source>Am J Pathol</source><year>2001</year><volume>159</volume><fpage>431</fpage><lpage>437</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11485901</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brognard</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name><name><surname>Ni</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>PDennis</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Akt/protein kinase B is constitutively active in non-small cell lung cancer cells and promotes cellular survival and resistance to chemotherapy and radiation</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>2001</year><volume>61</volume><fpage>3986</fpage><lpage>3997</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11358816</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hynes</surname><given-names>NE</given-names></name><name><surname>Lane</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>ERBB receptors and cancer: the complexity of targeted inhibitors</article-title><source>Nat Rev Cancer</source><year>2005</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>341</fpage><lpage>354</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15864276</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/nrc1609</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yamamoto</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Altschuler</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Wood</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Horlick</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacobs</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lapetina</surname><given-names>EG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Association of phosphorylated in